# Localization Files Completeness

## Rule

All vue-i18n new/changed string tokens in .vue files (example: `$t('pageInventory.systemIndicator.identifyLed')` ), must be added/updated to the primary English (en-US.json) file.
All localization files (specifically ru-RU.json and zh-CN.json) must contain all the keys that exist in the primary English (en-US.json) file.

## Why

Missing translation keys will cause parts of the UI to fall back to English or potentially display empty content for users using the Russian or Chinese localizations. This creates a poor user experience for non-English speaking users.

## How to Fix

1. Add any missing keys to the localization files
2. Use the "scripts/validate-translations.js" script, to identify missing keys

## Integration

Add this check to your CI pipeline or git pre-commit hooks:

```bash
node /scripts/validate-translations.js
```

## Notes

- The English file (en-US.json) is considered the primary source of truth
- All keys present in the English file must exist in all other translation files
